-- title:
--   §1 main result: MA existence, uniqueness, optimality and effective normalization
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal C=\langle H,S,\omega I\rangle$ be the exact 192-element single-qubit Clifford group, where $\omega=e^{i\pi/4}$, and add $T=\operatorname{diag}(1,\omega)$. Products act from right to left, and absolute phase is retained. Every operator generated by these gates has a unique expression
--
--   $$
--   (T\mid\varepsilon)(HT\mid SHT)^*C,\qquad C\in\mathcal C.
--   $$
--   The terminal is a Clifford operator, rather than a chosen Clifford spelling. The number of displayed $T$ letters is minimal among all exact Clifford+$T$ decompositions of that operator. A fixed finite suffix-rewrite algorithm converts every symbolic input of length $n$ to this expression with at most $B(n+1)$ primitive operations, for one input-independent constant $B>0$. Clifford table lookups and bounded stack operations have unit cost.
--
--   This packages existence, uniqueness, optimality and effective symbolic normalization. Matrix-input arithmetic complexity is separately inventoried in Theorem 5.1.
-- source:
--   Remarks on Matsumoto and Amano's normal form for single-qubit Clifford+T operators, arXiv:1312.6584v2, PDF p. 1, §1 main result: MA existence, uniqueness, optimality and effective normalization

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Gap48_P10

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P10

open scoped Classical BigOperators Pointwise

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P21 (Letter letterMatrix)

open QAlgorithms.QubitChannels (sigma)

-- Equation (1), PDF p.1: notation for Mathlib matrices, without a new declaration.

local notation "Mat" => Matrix Bool Bool ℂ

local notation "omega" => QAlgorithms.gateT true true

/-- Introduction, PDF p.1: existence, uniqueness, T-optimality and effective
symbolic normalization, with the input-independent linear algorithm of pp.2-3.
The matrix-input arithmetic bound is separately inventoried as Theorem 5.1. -/
theorem ma_main :
    (∀ U : Mat, CliffordT U → ∃! M : NormalForm, maValue M = U) ∧
    (∀ (M : NormalForm) (w : List Input), inputWordMatrix w = maValue M →
      normalTCount M ≤ inputTCount w) ∧
    LinearNormalizer maTokens maValue := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P10

end
